join Dumi (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
update Dumi (Aggravated)
- Long day?
	Hope: Long day?
	Dumi: Walked to Ga-Kgapane and back to stand in a yard for two hours so somebody else could get roofing sheets at a fair price.
	- What do you get out of it?
		Hope: What do you get out of it?
		Dumi: Nothing. I now owe the man a favour, which I'll pay some time, probably at an inconvenient moment.
	- You could have taken a cut
		Hope: You could have taken a cut.
		Dumi: No.
		Dumi: The moment I take a cut, every trade I broker gets looked at twice. 'What's Dumi getting.' And then people stop asking me, and then they take bad deals on their own.
		Dumi: Sorry. That's the one thing I get sharp about.
	- Don't apologise
		Hope: Don't apologise.
		Dumi: Mm. Well.
		Dumi: It cost me a day and a favour. The family got a roof that doesn't leak. That's a good exchange rate.
[signal arg="hearts:dumi:1"]
set {GameState.dumi_favor_seen} = true
